Suppose x = 1, y = -1, and z = 1. What will be displayed by the following statement?

```python
x = 2; y = 2; z = 2
if x > 0:
  if y > 0:
    print("x > 0 and y > 0")
  elif z > 0:
    print("x < 0 and z > 0")
```

A) x > 0 and y > 0 B) x < 0 and z < 0 C) Nothing is displayed D) The program won't run because of syntax error
